2|0@xboxone^1440780100#cuis4w8:BenChandler$:My thoughts so far: The parkour feels more tacked on than the CoD campaigns. I've gone entire matches without ever using them or even seeing other people make use of them. Still no dedicated servers (if the constant host migrations and disconnections are anything to go by). Not a fan of being forced to use preset characters. Say what you will about CoD: aw, but being able to completely customize the look of your character was a really nice addition. Was hoping BO3 would move forward with customization (especially since there are augmented soldiers now), but instead they've gone and cut out nearly all character customization (this does not include loadouts and weapons). Custom paint for your weapons is an okay addition, but it doesn't make up for the overall lack of character customization. It's also nice that our characters have bodies in-game now (that even cast shadows!). I thought someone was sneaking up behind me when I saw a shadow on the wall so I freaked out and turned around spraying everywhere only for their to be no one. I looked back, realized it was my shadow, then I looked down and realized I had a body. We're finally no longer floating cameras with arms. So overall impression, I'm not sold on it. Compared to Halo 5, this just feels lacking in comparison, and with all the games coming out near the end of the year, BO3 is going to be one of the games I'm skipping out on. 
